.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt PASSGEN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm passgen
.Nd Generate pseudorandom passphrases
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p Ar path
.Op Fl w Ar count
.Op Fl c Ar max
.Op Fl n Ar max
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
Generates a pseudorandom passphrase using a given wordlist.
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
reads its wordlist from
.Pa /usr/local/share/dict/wordlist .
Alternative wordlists can be specified by 
.Fl p .
The wordlist must follow the format of
.Lk https://www.eff.org/files/2016/07/18/eff_large_wordlist.txt "EFF's large wordlist" ,
with each entry consisting of a numeric identifier and a word.
.Pp
Words may randomly get capitalized.
The value specified by
.Fl c
sets an upper bound to the number of capitalized words.
.Pp
Words may randomly get appended by a number randomly selected between 0-9.
The value specified by
.Fl n
sets an upper bound to the number of words that may get appended by a number.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar path
This option specifies the path of the wordlist.
Defaults to
.Pa /usr/local/share/dict/wordlist .
.It Fl w Ar count
This option specifies the number of words in the passphrase.
The minimum value is 3.
The default value is 5.
.It Fl c Ar max
This option specifies the maximum number of capitalized words.
The default is half the number of words.
.It Fl n Ar max
This option specifies the maximum number of words that may be appended by a number.
The default is the value specified by
.Fl c .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr awk 1 ,
.Xr jot 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Armin Shirazi Aq Mt sharmeanix@tutamail.com
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.Nm
uses
.Xr sort 1
.Fl R
flag to pick the words.
.Pp
Random number generation is done via
.Xr jot 1
when available.
Otherwise, the
.Fn rand
function from
.Xr awk 1
is used.
.Xr awk 1
is seeded with four bytes read from
.Pa /dev/urandom
followed by the PID of
.Nm .
